# Pinned SSH host keys for the deploy hosts, consumed by
# .github/actions/kamal-deploy-setup. Without a matching entry that action falls
# back to trust-on-first-use and prints a warning annotation on every deploy.
#
# To populate, from a machine already on the Tailnet:
#
#   ssh-keyscan nadeshiko >> .github/known_hosts
#
# Use plain `ssh-keyscan`, not `ssh-keyscan -H`: the action matches the host name
# at the start of the line, which hashing would hide. Verify the fingerprints
# against the host itself before committing (`ssh-keygen -lf` on the pasted keys
# vs `ssh-keygen -lf /etc/ssh/ssh_host_*_key.pub` on the server) — pinning a key
# you learned over the same untrusted channel proves nothing.
#
# Replace the keys here whenever the host is rebuilt or its keys are rotated.
